    "work": "The Nuclear Company and Palantir are building a digital “mission control” for fleets of nuclear construction projects. A remote expert team would monitor budget, productivity, quality, and schedule through a shared data layer with LLMs, AI, and predictive analytics. Site teams would receive live guidance on supply-chain delays and corrective actions; drones and lidar would identify weld deviations rapidly; and regulators would receive real-time traceability into decisions and changes. Webb states targets to halve budget and delivery time and reduce peak labor from 10,000 to 5,000 while improving safety.",
    "entities": "The Nuclear Company; Jonathan Webb; Palantir; Palantir AIP; AIPCon 8; U.S. nuclear industry; U.S. nuclear regulator; lidar; large language models.",
